course: dictionary
lesson: 1663
title: Chlorinate: making water safe
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words tell you how something is made clean and safe. Chlorinate is one of them, and the sentences around it give clues. Look at this one: «The water in the pool is chlorinated to keep it clean.» Pools are for swimming, and the words to keep it clean tell you that the water is being made free of germs.
explain: Look at the word's ending. Chlorine is a chemical, and chlorinate means to add chlorine. Now read this: «...carry chlorinated fresh water (cleaned with a chemical called chlorine), not sea water.» The brackets explain the word for you: chlorinated water is water cleaned with chlorine.
explain: To check your meaning, swap it into the sentence. "The water in the pool has had chlorine added to keep it clean" still makes sense, so your meaning works. When the brackets and the clues agree, you can be confident.
fact: Chlorinate is a verb: chlorinate, chlorinates, chlorinated, chlorinating.
fact: «Chlorinate» means to add chlorine to water to kill germs and make it safe for drinking or swimming.
fact: «Chlorinated» water is water that has had chlorine added to it.
fact: In chemistry, to chlorinate a substance means to combine it with chlorine.
fact: Towns chlorinate drinking water, which has saved millions of lives by stopping diseases like cholera.
exercise: «The water in the pool is chlorinated to keep it clean.» What does chlorinated mean here? | *Has had chlorine added to kill germs | Has been filled with sea water | Has been heated until it is warm | Has been coloured blue
exercise: Towns chlorinate drinking water. Why do they do this? | To make it taste of salt | To make it run faster through the pipes | *To kill germs and make it safe to drink | To turn it into ice for cold drinks
exercise: In «...carry chlorinated fresh water (cleaned with a chemical called chlorine), not sea water», which word tells you how the water was cleaned? | fresh | sea | *chlorine | pipes
test: In chemistry, what does it mean to chlorinate a substance? | To paint it a bright colour | To freeze it into a solid | To dissolve it in sea water | *To combine it with chlorine
test: Yesterday the workers ___ the pool water. | *chlorinated | chlorinate | chlorine | chlorinates
exam: Why is swimming pool water chlorinated? | *To kill germs and keep it clean and safe | To make it sweeter to taste | To make it colder for swimmers | To turn it into sea water
